WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.588
Here's the route, in
the guide's run order.

2
00:00:02.588 --> 00:00:05.917
Scene one: the pilot
decides Internet Access on

3
00:00:05.917 --> 00:00:09.162
a feature whose GCC
availability isn't stated.

4
00:00:09.162 --> 00:00:11.987
Scene two: the logs leave a category out.

5
00:00:11.987 --> 00:00:15.100
Scene three: one device
is behind the rest.

6
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.693
Scene four: sign-ins
are short of the target,

7
00:00:17.693 --> 00:00:20.137
and the first change goes through a plan.

8
00:00:20.137 --> 00:00:23.464
Scene five: the compliant
network policy isn't ready,

9
00:00:23.464 --> 00:00:25.862
and a partner tenant isn't registered.

10
00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:29.438
Scene six: a Finance app
that's really a VPN again.

11
00:00:29.438 --> 00:00:33.713
Scene seven: an expired bypass
and a certificate near expiry.

12
00:00:33.713 --> 00:00:36.812
Scene eight: the ring says no-go, then go.

13
00:00:36.812 --> 00:00:40.900
And scene nine runs the same
commands in test, then production.
